📊 WEEK-3 | DAY-6: Data Visualization with Matplotlib, Seaborn & Plotly

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 What is Data Visualization?

**Data Visualization** is the graphical representation of data to:

* Understand patterns & trends
* Identify relationships
* Detect outliers & anomalies
* Communicate insights clearly

It is a critical step in **EDA (Exploratory Data Analysis)**.

---

🎯 Why Visualization is Important?

* Makes complex data easy to understand
* Reveals hidden patterns
* Helps in decision-making
* Improves storytelling with data
* Essential for Data Science & Analytics

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🖌️ Matplotlib

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What is Matplotlib?

**Matplotlib** is a low-level Python library used to create **static, customizable plots**.

It gives full control over plot elements.

---

Key Characteristics

* Highly customizable
* Static plots
* Base library for many other visualization tools
* Works well with NumPy & Pandas

---

Common Plot Types

* Line plot
* Bar chart
* Histogram
* Scatter plot
* Pie chart

---

When to Use Matplotlib?

* When you need full control over plots
* For publication-quality visuals
* For basic & custom visualizations

---

Limitations

* Verbose syntax
* Not interactive
* Styling requires more code

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎨 Seaborn

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What is Seaborn?

**Seaborn** is a high-level visualization library built on top of Matplotlib.

It is designed specifically for **statistical data visualization**.

---

Key Characteristics

* Cleaner and more attractive visuals
* Built-in themes & color palettes
* Integrates easily with Pandas DataFrames
* Focuses on statistical plots

---

Common Plot Types

* Box plot
* Violin plot
* Heatmap
* Pair plot
* Count plot
* Regression plot

---

When to Use Seaborn?

* For quick statistical analysis
* When working with DataFrames
* To visualize distributions & relationships
* For correlation & categorical analysis

---

Limitations

* Less control than Matplotlib
* Mostly static plots

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🌐 Plotly

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What is Plotly?

**Plotly** is a modern visualization library used to create **interactive and dynamic plots**.

It is widely used in dashboards and web applications.

---

Key Characteristics

* Interactive plots (zoom, hover, pan)
* Supports animations
* Works well with dashboards
* Web-friendly visuals

---

 Common Plot Types

* Interactive line & bar charts
* Scatter plots
* 3D plots
* Time-series plots
* Choropleth maps

---

When to Use Plotly?

* Interactive dashboards
* Web-based analytics
* Presentations requiring interactivity
* Large & complex datasets

---

Limitations

* Heavier than Matplotlib/Seaborn
* More complex syntax
* Requires browser rendering

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

